criteria.note:
All six decision items sit above the bar at 360x640:
- the worn hero, 77-386;
- the H1 (Cormorant 27), 398-426;
- the price row at 432-461: Rs 2,399 in Cormorant 24, the strike in 15 ink-2, 'incl. GST' and 'Surgical steel, PVD rhodium' in Jost 12;
- the ruled ladder, caption 471-487 and rungs 490-538;
- 'Free insured delivery, est. 18-20 Nov · COD available', 544-562;
- the bar from 575 (measure.json, probe.js).
Nothing wraps at 320, 360 or 412. The hierarchy runs photo, name, price, ladder, delivery, which is the right order.

Art faults:
- The ladder caption ends on a verb, 'this bracelet becomes', which dangles into a table (fix 6).
- At 320 the 11px rung labels run right up to the vertical rules with 0px clearance (lad320.js: label 2 ends at x 207, where the rule is; label 3 ends at 304, the gutter). At 360 the clearance is 4-5px.
- The photo is 48% of the screen. That is forced by the budget, not a fault.

The set is a calm, Missoma-like list (s2x_01-02):
- the ring first, as the rhodium match;
- full names in Cormorant 18, prices aligned right;
- FACTS metal lines, and '3 in stock' only where it is true;
- deep-sage marginal rupees and 88x44 Adds;
- a running summary that appears once the bag has something in it;
- an outlined 'Add all four · Rs 3,987'.
The sub-line now explains the pairing.

Art faults:
- With the bag empty, 'With the bracelet it adds / Rs 659, not Rs 999' wraps to two ragged lines in every row, beside a button. Rs 999 is printed twice per row.
- In the bag, a row says 'In your bag' next to a button that says 'IN BAG' (set_after.png).
- 'All four: 30% off the four pieces' says 'four' twice (fix 6).
- The thumbnails sit on three different grounds: terracotta, cream and grey. This is roadmap.

The 10-today set is met:
- a worn hero;
- slide 6 as an inline SVG ruler with the live caption '18 cm long · fits wrists 15-19 cm / Measure around your wrist bone.' (slide_5.png);
- 'Fits: Wrists of 15 to 19 cm' with a 'See the size guide' link to that slide;
- the FAQ answer to match.
Gaps:
- The ruler's own labels, 'fits wrists 15-19 cm' and '18 cm', repeat the caption word for word instead of saying which mark is the wrist and which is the bracelet (fix 8).
- No dimension photo yet (roadmap).

Honest and light:
- a 3.3 s cut that loads on tap;
- a mehendi poster;
- labelled on the slide, the tiles and in the viewer;
- 4:5 tiles with no ceiling fan.
Faults:
- The one short clip has four ways in: the hero chip, the slide 5 plate and both tiles. 'Creator collaboration' is printed five times. The disclosure starts to read as defensive padding.
- The second tile plays but has no Play plate, while the first has one.
- The captions are unequal: two lines against one. The second caption, 'Creator collaboration · Riya', is only a label and says nothing about the frame (fix 7).

Type and legibility (taps and contrast belong to the UX lens). The type is now a system:
- Cormorant 27/24/20/18/15 at weight 500 with lining figures;
- Jost 15/13/12/11;
- 22 text styles in the census, down from 34 in round 2, with no half pixels and a floor of 11px (probe.js);
- tracked caps only on buttons, folds, dt labels and the footer tagline, at .12-.14em.
Remaining issues:
- The 11px rung labels touch the rules at 320 (C1).
- The bag drawer's Cormorant 24 Total is cut below the drawer body with two pieces, so the price hierarchy loses its anchor (drawer_2.png, fix 4).

Restraint is real:
- two families;
- ivory, ivory-deep, ink, ink-2 and deep sage only (sage, gold and blush are declared but never used);
- radius 0 except the bag's checkout;
- no badges or stars;
- one ink primary;
- a 48px section rhythm;
- the deep-sage footer.
Next to the bench folds it now sits with Mejuri, not with GIVA or Palmonas.

What still looks heavy or templated:
- The first scroll opens on the reassurance list: three paragraphs at full body size in full ink, each behind a stroke icon (s2x_01). That is the Shopify icon-with-text block, and it is visually louder than the set sub-line beneath it (fix 3).
- The hero chip is a 200px text plate on the photo (fix 1).
- Slide 5 has three plates.
- The Google, PhonePe and Paytm marks on Buy now are the only saturated colour outside the photos. They are kept for CRO reasons, but they are the loudest pixels on the first screen.

The shape is right (added.png, added_ring.png):
- '✓ Added to bag', then 'View bag · Rs total';
- the badge count;
- a card over the photo that confirms the bracelet first;
- one suggestion in rupees ('Adds Rs 659, not Rs 999 / 10% off both');
- an inert ink '✓ ADDED';
- no timer;
- the price, ladder and delivery line never covered;
- 'Keep browsing' and 'See the whole set'.
Art faults:
- The bracelet thumbnail is 40px wide and the ring's is 48px, so the two names start at different x: 77 and 85 CSS px.
- After the ring is added the card ends at 354, over the counter plate at 349-376. The card's bottom border cuts across the '1 / 7' plate.
- 'PVD rhodium, like the / bracelet' leaves 'bracelet' alone on its own line (fix 2).

fixes.change:
Make the chip name the clip, not the photo it sits on, by putting Riya's own frame inside it.

1. Crop i/reel1.jpg (Riya's mehendi wrist, real Naira media) to i/chip-riya.jpg at 80x104 (2x of 40x52), centred on the wrist at about 40% from the top. It is about 3 KB.

2. Markup:
<button class="plate chip" id="chip" hidden aria-label="Play Riya's clip, a creator collaboration"><img class="th" src="i/chip-riya.jpg" width="40" height="52" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="low"><span class="tt"><b><svg viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 0l9 5-9 5z"/></svg><span id="chipt">Riya's clip</span></b><span>Creator collaboration</span></span></button>

3. CSS:
.chip { height: 52px; padding: 0 12px 0 0; gap: 10px; }
.chip .th { width: 40px; height: 52px; object-fit: cover; }
.chip .tt { display: grid; line-height: 15px; }
.chip .tt b { font-weight: 500; font-size: var(--t-label); letter-spacing: .04em; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
.chip .tt b svg { width: 8px; height: 8px; }
.chip .tt > span { font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--t-micro); color: var(--ink-2); }

4. When an angle line replaces the text (L791), hide .th and the second line.

Measured on a copy (mock_fold_360.png, mock_folds_320_412.jpg): the chip is 165x52, 35px narrower than today. It sits at 10-175 x 324-376 at 360x640, y 252-304 at 320x568 and y 416-468 at 412x732. It stays clear of the stones and the counter, and the facts do not move.

The words match the trust lens's round-3 text ('Riya's clip · creator collaboration'), split over two lines.

Turn the three paragraphs into a bold lead plus quiet detail. The words stay exactly as they are; only the weight changes.

Markup:
- '<b>Waterproof and tarnish free.</b> Daily wear and water are fine.'
- '<b>Faulty piece?</b> Tell us on WhatsApp within 7 days of delivery, with photos, for a repair, replacement or store credit. <u>The policy</u>'
- '<b>Questions before you buy?</b>' followed by the two links as now.

CSS:
.assure li { font-size: var(--t-small); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-2); padding: 11px 0; }
.assure li b { font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
.assure .l44 { color: var(--ink); }
.assure .ask .links { margin-top: -10px; }
.assure svg { margin-top: 1px; }

Measured on a copy (mock_scr2.png): the list goes from 249 to 222px, and the set heading rises to y 824. ink-2 at 13px on ivory is about 6.9:1.

Give each bag item the set rows' idiom.

Markup per item:
<div class="top2"><div class="n">name</div><span class="pr rs">price</span></div><div class="m">metal</div><div class="ctl"><span class="step">...</span><button class="rm">Remove</button></div>

CSS:
.dr-items li { padding: 12px 0; }
.top2 { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; }
.dr-items .ctl { margin-top: 6px; }

This puts the name and price on one line, and the stepper and Remove on the next. Remove keeps its 44px minimum.

Measured on a copy (mock_drawer.png): each item goes from 162 to 123px. With two pieces the Cormorant 24 'Total Rs 3,058' sits at 450-496, above the footer at 540. Today it is cut below the visible body (drawer_2.png).
